{{- /*
capabilities.tmpl — reads THIS chezmoi command's capability snapshot. It probes
nothing itself.

WHAT THIS IS FOR. A `transient-blocking` site (see skip.sh.tmpl) exits 0, so
chezmoi records it as a successful run. It can only re-run on its own if the
script's RENDERED CONTENT changes when the missing precondition appears. This
partial emits a two-valued token for exactly that purpose; the caller hashes it
through fingerprint.tmpl's `values` key, so the token flipping changes the
script's content and chezmoi re-runs it.

WHY A PROBE AND NOT A MARKER FILE. Measured on chezmoi v2.71.0 against a scratch
source and destination:

  marker whose content changes on each skip  -> script re-runs on EVERY apply
                                                (an always-run script)
  marker with stable content                 -> ran twice, then stalled
                                                permanently, and did NOT re-run
                                                when the precondition appeared
  probe of the precondition                  -> ran once, byte-stable across
                                                three further applies, re-ran
                                                immediately once the
                                                precondition appeared

WHERE THE VALUE COMES FROM NOW. The probe used to run here, one subprocess per
CALL, on every chezmoi command. The converted tree names ~34 distinct probes
across ~57 blocking sites, so that form cost ~57 subprocesses per `status` or
`diff`, and two renders inside one command could disagree. Resolution moved to
the `read-source-state.pre` hook (.install-prerequisites.sh,
`write_capability_cache`), which resolves every registry entry ONCE, before the
source state is read, and publishes:

  ${XDG_CACHE_HOME:-~/.cache}/chezmoi/capabilities/<identity>.tsv   0600, in a 0700 dir

  line 1   capability-cache-v1 <TAB> identity <TAB> owner pid <TAB> start marker <TAB> registry sha256
  line n   <registry key> <TAB> available|unavailable        (in registry order)

THE ARGUMENT CONTRACT DID NOT CHANGE. Call sites written against the old probe
form stay correct: a dict with `ctx` and `probe`, `available`/`unavailable` out,
no trailing newline, safe as a fingerprint.tmpl value.

THE RECORD IS PER COMMAND, NOT PER HOST. `<identity>` is a SHA-256 over the
NUL-delimited schema, the chezmoi process's PID, and that PID's immutable start
marker (.chezmoitemplates/capability-cache-identity.sh, shared verbatim with the
hook). Each read below resolves it through one `output "sh" "-c"` child whose own
$PPID *is* that chezmoi process, so reader and writer agree while two simultaneous
`chezmoi apply` runs with identical arguments get different records. That single
`sh` is not a capability probe: it computes an identity and touches no host state.

WHY A MISSING OR MISMATCHED RECORD IS `unavailable` AND NOT AN ERROR. A render
with no hook — `chezmoi execute-template` under the AGENTS.md stub-`op` recipe, the
CI render-internals job, any fixture that bypasses the hook — has no record for its
identity. `unavailable` is the fail-safe direction: it renders the skip branch, which
is what those isolated renders want. It cannot fail open, because a capability is
only ever a fingerprint input. A record that IS present but does not match this
command (other identity, other registry digest, prior schema, wrong key set, wrong
token shape) is treated exactly like an absent one, so a stale record can never
publish a token. When the hook DID run, integrity faults were already fatal there:
the hook exits non-zero before any template renders.

An unknown probe name is still a hard render failure — that is a call-site bug, and
the registry is the enumeration of what exists.

THIS IS DELIBERATELY NOT THE FACT REGISTRY. `.chezmoidata/facts.yaml:5-9` excludes
momentary state — a live D-Bus session, a `sudo -n` credential cache — from host
IDENTITY, and that exclusion stands. A capability here:

  - never appears in a `gates:` expression and never gates anything,
  - is consumed only as a fingerprint input, so it can only ever change WHEN a
    script re-runs, never WHETHER it is allowed to act,
  - therefore cannot fail open, which is the property facts.yaml's per-fact
    `whenFalse:` doctrine exists to protect.

Adding a capability is adding a row to .chezmoidata/.capability-registry.tsv plus
its reviewed resolver kind in the hook — never a `gates:` consumer, and never an
inline command at a call site.

ARGUMENT — a dict:

  {{ includeTemplate "capabilities.tmpl" (dict "ctx" . "probe" "sudo-usable") }}
*/ -}}
{{- if not (kindIs "map" .) -}}
{{-   fail (printf "capabilities.tmpl: expected a dict, got a %s (%v). Call it as {{ includeTemplate \"capabilities.tmpl\" (dict \"ctx\" . \"probe\" \"sudo-usable\") }}" (kindOf .) .) -}}
{{- end -}}
{{- $probe := "" -}}{{- if hasKey . "probe" -}}{{- $probe = .probe -}}{{- end -}}

{{- /* The registry is the enumeration of known probes AND the thing the record's
   digest is taken over. Its basename is dot-prefixed because chezmoi discovers
   .chezmoidata/ recursively and aborts every command with ".tsv: unknown format"
   on a visible unknown-format data file (v2.71.0), while dot-prefixed entries are
   skipped — which is what this file needs: it is read as raw bytes here and in the
   hook, and must never merge into the template data map. Keep this path
   byte-identical to CAPABILITY_REGISTRY_RELPATH in .install-prerequisites.sh. */ -}}
{{- $registryPath := joinPath .ctx.chezmoi.sourceDir ".chezmoidata" ".capability-registry.tsv" -}}
{{- if not (stat $registryPath) -}}
{{-   fail (printf "capabilities.tmpl: missing capability registry %s. It is the only runtime source of probe keys; restore it from source control." $registryPath) -}}
{{- end -}}
{{- $registryRaw := include $registryPath -}}
{{- /* SHAPE-CHECK BEFORE TRUSTING IT, exactly as facts.tmpl does with its cache: a
   truncated registry must produce an actionable diagnostic, not a mis-parsed key
   set that silently turns every probe into `unavailable`. */ -}}
{{- if not (regexMatch "^capability-registry-v1\n([a-z0-9][a-z0-9.-]*\t[a-z-]+\t[a-z-]+\tavailable\tunavailable\n)+$" $registryRaw) -}}
{{-   fail (printf "capabilities.tmpl: capability registry %s is malformed. Expected the capability-registry-v1 header followed by sorted <key>\\t<kind>\\t<side-effect>\\tavailable\\tunavailable rows." $registryPath) -}}
{{- end -}}
{{- $registryDigest := $registryRaw | sha256sum -}}
{{- $known := list -}}
{{- range $row := splitList "\n" (trimSuffix "\n" $registryRaw) -}}
{{-   if ne $row "capability-registry-v1" -}}
{{-     $known = append $known (index (splitList "\t" $row) 0) -}}
{{-   end -}}
{{- end -}}
{{- if not (has $probe $known) -}}
{{-   fail (printf "capabilities.tmpl: unknown probe %q. Known probes: %s. Declare a new probe in %s with its reviewed resolver kind rather than inlining a command at the call site, so every probe stays enumerable in one place." $probe (join ", " $known) $registryPath) -}}
{{- end -}}

{{- /* Identity of the command doing this render. The `sh` child's $PPID is the
   chezmoi process; the helper is read as RAW BYTES (not includeTemplate: it is
   shell, and a brace sequence in it must never be parsed as a template action) and
   embedded verbatim, so reader and hook cannot drift. The helper always exits 0 (a
   non-zero `output` child would abort the render) and says `unresolved` when it
   cannot derive an identity. */ -}}
{{- $identityHelper := joinPath .ctx.chezmoi.sourceDir ".chezmoitemplates" "capability-cache-identity.sh" -}}
{{- if not (stat $identityHelper) -}}
{{-   fail (printf "capabilities.tmpl: missing identity helper %s. The hook and this partial must derive the same identity from the same bytes; restore it from source control." $identityHelper) -}}
{{- end -}}
{{- $identityLine := output "sh" "-c" (printf "CAPABILITY_CACHE_OWNER_PID=\"$PPID\"\nexport CAPABILITY_CACHE_OWNER_PID\n%s" (include $identityHelper)) | trim -}}
{{- $token := "unavailable" -}}
{{- $identityFields := splitList "\t" $identityLine -}}
{{- if eq (len $identityFields) 4 -}}
{{-   $identity := index $identityFields 3 -}}
{{-   $ownerPid := index $identityFields 1 -}}
{{-   $marker := index $identityFields 2 -}}
{{- /* Same path the hook writes. `env` reads the same XDG_CACHE_HOME the hook
     read, and .chezmoi.homeDir is the same $HOME — no extra subprocess. */ -}}
{{-   $cacheHome := env "XDG_CACHE_HOME" -}}
{{-   if eq $cacheHome "" -}}
{{-     $cacheHome = joinPath .ctx.chezmoi.homeDir ".cache" -}}
{{-   end -}}
{{-   $recordPath := joinPath $cacheHome "chezmoi" "capabilities" (printf "%s.tsv" $identity) -}}
{{-   $recordStat := stat $recordPath -}}
{{- /* A record must be a regular file whose mode is exactly 0600 — mode 384 with
     no type bits set. `stat` follows symlinks and cannot report ownership, so the
     real containment is the hook's owner-only 0700 directory; this rejects the
     shapes a template CAN see. */ -}}
{{-   if and $recordStat (eq $recordStat.type "file") (eq (printf "%v" $recordStat.mode) "384") -}}
{{-     $raw := include $recordPath -}}
{{-     if regexMatch "^capability-cache-v1\t[0-9a-f]+\t[0-9]+\t[A-Za-z0-9:._-]+\t[0-9a-f]+\n([a-z0-9][a-z0-9.-]*\t(available|unavailable)\n)+$" $raw -}}
{{-       $rows := splitList "\n" (trimSuffix "\n" $raw) -}}
{{-       $header := splitList "\t" (index $rows 0) -}}
{{- /* Provenance: this identity, this command's PID and start marker, and the
         digest of the registry bytes just validated above. Any mismatch means the
         record belongs to another command or another registry. */ -}}
{{-       if and (eq (index $header 1) $identity) (eq (index $header 2) $ownerPid) (eq (index $header 3) $marker) (eq (index $header 4) $registryDigest) -}}
{{-         $cached := dict -}}
{{-         range $row := slice $rows 1 (len $rows) -}}
{{-           $fields := splitList "\t" $row -}}
{{-           $_ := set $cached (index $fields 0) (index $fields 1) -}}
{{-         end -}}
{{- /* EXACT key set, both directions: a record missing a key would hand that
           consumer a silent default, and an extra key means the record was written
           against a registry this render did not validate. */ -}}
{{-         $complete := eq (len (keys $cached)) (len $known) -}}
{{-         range $key := $known -}}
{{-           if not (hasKey $cached $key) -}}
{{-             $complete = false -}}
{{-           end -}}
{{-         end -}}
{{-         if $complete -}}
{{-           $token = index $cached $probe -}}
{{-         end -}}
{{-       end -}}
{{-     end -}}
{{-   end -}}
{{- end -}}
{{- $token -}}
